@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `hvac-nouns`
IMPORT `hvac-fees-regs`
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`

-- hvac-law-s63-commencement.l4 -- Law s 63: commencement and application.
--
-- Written before the Second Schedule because three rows of the Schedule hang off it ("this
-- provision shall remain in force for three years from the commencement of this Law under
-- s 63(a)(1)").  Text quoted from Hebrew Wikisource rev 2947808 (unofficial) and checked by
-- eye against the official gazette, Sefer HaChukim 3349 p. 182ff (where s 63 is on p. 197).

-- THE COUNTING.  "Three months from its publication" and "18 months from the Commencement Day" are
-- periods of months fixed "from" a day.  Interpretation Law 5741-1981 s 10(b) says how they are
-- counted: a period of months or years after an event ends "ביום שמספרו בחודש כמספר יום האירוע"
-- (on the day whose number in the month is the number of the day of the event), or on the month's
-- last day if it lacks that day; the last day is inside the period.  Every such period below goes
-- through the functions of il-interpretation-time.l4 (the Interpretation row's module, vendored
-- unchanged), and not through `add months`.
--
-- WHAT A COMMENCEMENT "N UNITS FROM" AN EVENT IS (fork F-C3).  s 10 fixes the last day of the
-- period.  A commencement "18 months from the Commencement Day" is taken to fall on that last day
-- (the day the period ends), so the Law commences on 16 January 2027.  The alternative is the day
-- AFTER the period ends, 17 January 2027; s 10 does not say which day of a period a commencement
-- names, and the unofficial annotation on the regulations' own commencement (16.7.2025 for
-- "7 days from" 9.7.2025) takes the last day.
--
-- s 10(c) (days of rest do not end a period) is NOT applied to a commencement day (fork F-X3):
-- nothing is done on the day a statute begins to bind, so there is no act whose last day a rest
-- day could cut short.  The functions marked "if s 10(c) applied" show the other reading, with
-- the calendar of days of rest as an input.

§ `Section 63: Commencement and application`

-- The gazette issue that published the Law:
-- 14 בינואר 2025 3349 י"ד בטבת התשפ"ה
-- (the Knesset passed it on 8 January 2025, "ח' בטבת התשפ"ה"; the issue is dated 14 January 2025.)
@ref Law s 63(a)(1), "מיום פרסומו"; Sefer HaChukim 3349
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the Law was published` MEANS YMD 2025 1 14

-- s 63(a)(1): "שלושה חודשים מיום פרסומו או מועד כניסתן לתוקף של תקנות לפי סעיף 59, לפי המאוחר"
-- (א) תחילתו של חוק זה, למעט פרק ו׳ –
-- (1) לעניין ביצוע עבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר הפועלת באמצעות קרר דליק המנוי בתוספת הרביעית, ובלבד שהשימוש בו הותר על פי כל דין – שלושה חודשים מיום פרסומו או מועד כניסתן לתוקף של תקנות לפי סעיף 59, לפי המאוחר (להלן – יום התחילה); השר, לאחר התייעצות עם השר להגנת הסביבה, רשאי לשנות, בצו, את התוספת הרביעית;
-- s 63(a)(2):
-- (2) לעניין ביצוע עבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר הפועלת באמצעות קרר שאינו כאמור בפסקה (1) – 18 חודשים מיום התחילה.
-- s 63(b):
-- (ב) תחילתו של פרק ו׳ 18 חודשים מיום התחילה או במועד כניסתן לתוקף של תקנות לפי סעיף 46, לפי המאוחר.

-- The regulations under s 59 are the Fees Regulations.  They entered into force seven days
-- from publication in Kovetz HaTakanot 11951 (9 July 2025), that is 16 July 2025 (regulation
-- 5, see hvac-fees-regs.l4).  "The date of entry into force" is the first such regulations'.
@ref Law s 63(a)(1), "מועד כניסתן לתוקף של תקנות לפי סעיף 59"
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the regulations under section 59 entered into force` MEANS
    `the day the principal regulations commenced`

@ref Law s 63(a)(1): "לפי המאוחר"; s 63(b)
GIVEN a IS A DATE
      b IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later of` a `and` b MEANS
    IF a AT LEAST b THEN a ELSE b

-- THE FORK AT THE HEART OF s 63(a)(1) (F-C1).  The sentence is "three months from the day of
-- its publication or [the] date of entry into force of regulations under section 59,
-- whichever is later".  Two readings, with different answers:
--   B (taken):  the later of (publication + 3 months) and (the regulations' entry into force)
--               = the later of 14 April 2025 and 16 July 2025 = 16 July 2025.
--   A:          three months after the later of (publication) and (the regulations' entry
--               into force) = 16 October 2025.
-- B is taken because s 63(b), drafted in the same breath, says in terms "18 months from the
-- Commencement Day OR ON the date of entry into force of regulations under s 46, whichever is
-- later" ("או במועד כניסתן לתוקף"): the later of a period's end and a date.  Section (a)(1)
-- drops the "ב" of "במועד", which is what leaves A open.  The unofficial consolidation
-- annotates (a)(1) only with the date the regulations commenced (16.7.2025), which does not
-- decide it.  Reading A is kept as its own function so that a reviewer can see the difference.
@ref Law s 63(a)(1), "יום התחילה" (the Commencement Day), reading B; Interpretation Law s 10(b)
GIVETH A DATE
`the Commencement Day` MEANS
    `the later of`
        (`s 10 — the last day of a period of` 3 `months from the day` `the day the Law was published`)
        `and`
        `the day the regulations under section 59 entered into force`

@ref Law s 63(a)(1), "יום התחילה" (the Commencement Day), reading A; Interpretation Law s 10(b)
GIVETH A DATE
`the Commencement Day on the other reading` MEANS
    `s 10 — the last day of a period of` 3 `months from the day`
        (`the later of` `the day the Law was published` `and` `the day the regulations under section 59 entered into force`)

-- The Commencement Day if s 10(c) were applied to the three-month period (the regulations'
-- entry into force is a date, not a counted period, and is not moved).
@ref Law s 63(a)(1); Interpretation Law s 10(b), (c)
GIVEN rest IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`the Commencement Day, if s 10(c) applied to a commencement day, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` rest MEANS
    `the later of`
        (`s 10(b), (c) — the last day of a period of` 3 `months after an event on` `the day the Law was published` `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` rest)
        `and`
        `the day the regulations under section 59 entered into force`

-- s 63(a)(1) and (a)(2) divide the work by the refrigerant.  A refrigerant on the Fourth
-- Schedule list whose use is NOT permitted by law is not "as stated in paragraph (1)", so it
-- falls to (a)(2) (fork F-C2); the Fourth Schedule itself is not encoded.
DECLARE `Class of work for commencement` IS ONE OF
    `work on a system using a listed flammable refrigerant whose use is permitted by law`
    `work on a system using any other refrigerant`

@ref Law s 63(a)(1) and (2)
GIVEN r IS A Refrigerant
GIVETH A `Class of work for commencement`
`the class of work for commencement of` r MEANS
    IF       r's `listed as a flammable refrigerant in the Fourth Schedule`
         AND r's `its use is permitted by law`
    THEN `work on a system using a listed flammable refrigerant whose use is permitted by law`
    ELSE `work on a system using any other refrigerant`

-- When the Law commences for a class of work.
@ref Law s 63(a)(1): "יום התחילה"; s 63(a)(2): "18 חודשים מיום התחילה"; Interpretation Law s 10(b)
GIVEN c IS A `Class of work for commencement`
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the Law commences for` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `work on a system using a listed flammable refrigerant whose use is permitted by law` THEN `the Commencement Day`
    WHEN `work on a system using any other refrigerant`                                         THEN `s 10 — the last day of a period of` 18 `months from the day` `the Commencement Day`

-- The same, if s 10(c) were applied to a commencement day.  For work on any other refrigerant the
-- nominal day, 16 January 2027, is a Saturday: with Saturday a day of rest the Law would
-- commence on Sunday 17 January 2027.
@ref Law s 63(a)(1), (2); Interpretation Law s 10(b), (c)
GIVEN c    IS A `Class of work for commencement`
      rest IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the Law commences for` c `, if s 10(c) applied to a commencement day, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` rest MEANS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `work on a system using a listed flammable refrigerant whose use is permitted by law` THEN `the Commencement Day, if s 10(c) applied to a commencement day, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` rest
    WHEN `work on a system using any other refrigerant`                                         THEN `s 10(b), (c) — the last day of a period of` 18 `months after an event on` (`the Commencement Day, if s 10(c) applied to a commencement day, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` rest) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` rest

-- Is the Law in force, for work on a system with that refrigerant, on a day?  Before it
-- commences the Law has nothing to say; that is the law's own answer, an ordinary value, and
-- not a refusal.
@ref Law s 63(a)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      r IS A Refrigerant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Law is in force on` d `for work on a system using` r MEANS
    d AT LEAST `the day the Law commences for` (`the class of work for commencement of` r)

-- s 63(b): Chapter 6 (administrative enforcement) commences 18 months from the Commencement
-- Day or on the day regulations under s 46 enter into force, whichever is later.  The sources
-- contain no regulations under s 46, so when they entered into force is an input: NOTHING means
-- none has entered into force, and then the chapter has no commencement day yet.
@ref Law s 63(b); Interpretation Law s 10(b)
GIVEN `the day regulations under section 46 entered into force` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day Chapter 6 commences, if section 46 regulations entered into force on` `the day regulations under section 46 entered into force` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day regulations under section 46 entered into force`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST x  THEN JUST (`the later of` (`s 10 — the last day of a period of` 18 `months from the day` `the Commencement Day`) `and` x)

@ref Law s 63(b)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the day regulations under section 46 entered into force` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Chapter 6 is in force on` d `if section 46 regulations entered into force on` `the day regulations under section 46 entered into force` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day Chapter 6 commences, if section 46 regulations entered into force on` `the day regulations under section 46 entered into force`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST c  THEN d AT LEAST c

-- A GAP.  s 63(a) fixes commencement "as regards the performance of work on a system" and
-- by refrigerant.  It does not say from when the licensing machinery itself -- the Registrar's
-- duty to give licences (s 6), licence terms (s 8), temporary licences (s 9), the duties of
-- ss 16 and 17 -- operates, and none of those is about a system's refrigerant.  The encoding
-- does not invent a date; the modules for those sections apply without a commencement gate,
-- and this is the question they leave open.
@ref Law s 63(a): commencement is stated only "לעניין ביצוע עבודה במערכת"
GIVETH A DATE
`the day from which the licensing provisions of sections 6, 8, 9, 16 and 17 operate` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 63(a) states commencement only as regards the performance of work on a system, by refrigerant, and does not say from when the licensing machinery of sections 6, 8, 9, 16 and 17 operates"
